ay go to CH05 (limitations - different therapy type).\n\nP0139: 2025 NSCLC immunotherapy resistance review. Good for CH03 (resistance mechanisms) and CH04 (intervention strategies).\n\nP0140: 2026 review on microbiome and metabolic health. Not cancer-specific. Limited direct relevance. May go to CH03 (general mechanisms) or CH05.\n\nP0141: 2023 review on CRC genetics and microbiome. Good for CH02 (CRC-specific taxa) and CH03 (mechanisms in CRC).\n\nP0142: 2025 review on optimizing cancer treatment through microbiome modulation. Good for CH04 (interventions) and CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0143: 2024 CBM588 probiotic in mRCC abstract. Microbiome changes, not efficacy. Good for CH04 (interventions) and CH02 (microbiome modulation).\n\nP0144: 2026 review on microbiome control of ICI response. Good for CH03 (mechanisms) and CH04 (FMT translation).\n\nP0145: 2026 review on microbiome-gut-liver axis in cancer immunotherapy. HCC-focused. Good for CH03 (mechanisms) and CH02 (liver cancer taxa).\n\nP0146: 2025 npj Biofilms and Microbiomes review on gut microbiota shaping immunotherapy responses. Good for CH02 (taxa) and CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0147: 2026 review on tumor-associated depression, gut microbiota, and ICI sensitivity. Psychoneuroimmunology angle. Good for CH03 (mechanisms - gut-brain-immune axis) and CH05 (emerging factors).\n\nP0148: 2023 KRAS-mutated NSCLC microbiome study. Specific subtype. Good for CH02 (subtype-specific taxa) and CH01 (clinical evidence).\n\nP0149: 2026 JEM abstract on ICI-induced myocarditis mechanism (TNF/CD8). No microbiome. Limited relevance. May go to CH03 (toxicity mechanisms) or CH05.\n\nP0150: 2025 Frontiers in Immunology review on gut microbiome in solid tumor ICI responses. Good for CH02 (taxa), CH03 (mechanisms), and CH04 (interventions).\n\nP0151: 2024 Frontiers in Immunology review on microbiome in PDAC. Good for CH03 (PDAC mechanisms) and CH04 (PDAC interventions).\n\nP0152: 2026 review on natural polysaccharides as immune adjuvants. Diet/microbiome angle. Good for CH04 (dietary interventions) and CH03 (mechanisms).\n\nP0153: 2026 abstract on PEG bowel prep impact on ICI response. Negative factor. Good for CH01 (confounding factors) and CH03 (barrier mechanisms).\n\nP0154: 2025 review on microbiome in atopic dermatitis. Not cancer. Limited relevance. May go to CH03 (general immune mechanisms) or CH05.\n\nP0155: 2025 ASCO abstract on diet and ICI outcomes in NSCLC. Good for CH04 (dietary interventions) and CH02 (diet-microbiome links).\n\nP0156: 2025 systematic review on dietary interventions and immunotherapy outcomes. Good for CH04 (diet evidence) and CH03 (diet-microbiome-immune mechanisms).\n\nP0157: 2023 review on overcoming ICI resistance. Good for CH03 (resistance mechanisms) and CH04 (combination strategies).\n\nP0158: 2019 review on melanoma ICI resistance mechanisms. Good for CH03 (melanoma-specific mechanisms) and CH02 (melanoma taxa).\n\nP0159: 2026 systematic review on gut microbiomes in skin cancer. Good for CH02 (skin cancer taxa",
